WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.562
Why does this chapter matter?

2
00:00:01.562 --> 00:00:06.131
Because the program gives every setting
one owning tool, and every server

3
00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:10.550
one patching tool, and both are
recorded in the configuration database.

4
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.275
Arc doesn't change any of that.

5
00:00:12.275 --> 00:00:15.536
What it does is turn the
server into an Azure resource,

6
00:00:15.536 --> 00:00:19.463
and from then on, tags tell Azure's
tools which servers are theirs.

7
00:00:19.463 --> 00:00:22.812
Those tags are written once,
at the moment of connection.

8
00:00:22.812 --> 00:00:27.437
So the onboarding run is the one place
owners get read, checked and carried.

9
00:00:27.437 --> 00:00:32.230
Connect a server without them, and it
belongs to whichever tool reaches it first.
